{"t": 0.9, "ns": "", "node": "supervisor", "type": "HumanMessage", "name": null, "content": "Using mace_md_specialist, run an NPT equilibration with run_nvt_md on the structure file /mnt/r3rerun/runs/gpt-4o-mini_4/out/nacl_water_box.xyz, using the MACE polar foundation model 'polar-1-m' (it loads by name itself, do NOT call download_mace_model). Use a starting box size of 12.5 Angstrom, temperature 300 K, pressure 1 bar (pressure_bar=1.0), 50 geometry-optimization steps first (minimize_steps=50), 14 MD steps, and save a trajectory frame every step (traj_interval=1). Save the trajectory to /mnt/r3rerun/runs/gpt-4o-mini_4/out/md.traj and the log to /mnt/r3rerun/runs/gpt-4o-mini_4/out/md.log. Then call check_density_convergence on that trajectory with window_frames=5 and tolerance_percent=0.05. If it reports that the density has not converged, run 16 more NPT MD steps with run_nvt_md, continuing from the trajectory at /mnt/r3rerun/runs/gpt-4o-mini_4/out/md.traj as the starting structure (same box size 12.5 Angstrom, temperature 300 K, pressure_bar=1.0, minimize_steps=0, traj_interval=1), saving to the same trajectory /mnt/r3rerun/runs/gpt-4o-mini_4/out/md.traj (overwrite) and log /mnt/r3rerun/runs/gpt-4o-mini_4/out/md.log, and then check convergence again. Keep extending in 16-step increments and re-checking until the check reports convergence. Once the density has converged, use dft_specialist to run a single-point electronic-structure calculation with run_dft_single_point on the final frame (frame_index=-1) of the trajectory at /mnt/r3rerun/runs/gpt-4o-mini_4/out/md.traj, using the GFN2-xTB method, charge=0, spin_multiplicity=1, and save the result to /mnt/r3rerun/runs/gpt-4o-mini_4/out/dft_single_point.json.  \nFirst use mace_md_specialist with run_nvt_md, then check_density_convergence. If needed, continue with run_nvt_md and check_density_convergence again, and finally use dft_specialist with run_dft_single_point.", "tool_calls": []}
